            "review_id": "REV_12597456_p1_0",
            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_0",
            "review_title": "Review at IZAKAYA Yen",
            "review_text": "Y&SFOOD!\nBangkok, Thailand1110 contributions\n0\nCasual & Proper Izakaya.\nOct 2024 • Solo\nDa Nang Dining Advice - Craving for Japanese food while in Asia is something we are all familiar with. Such desire can be satisfied only by tasting a wide range of small dishes, all different from each other, that can summarize Japanese approach to food in one dinner: izakaya.\nOur dinner at IZAKAYA YEN - @izakayayen - was the result of such craving and here are our picks:\n\n- Flame-Torched Tarako.\n\n- Cold Tofu.\n\n- Tamagoyaki.\n\n- Uni Sashimi.\n\n- Mix Chicken Offal Yakitori. \n\n- Soy-Marinated Quail Eggs.\n\n- Chicken Karaage.\n\nLike a proper Izakaya, IZAKAYA YEN welcomes diners with its counter seats, open Edo-Mae Sushi corner and Japanese greetings. \nThe place, tiny and cozy on the first floor, slightly enlarge on the second floor offering more tables and seats.\nBroad Izakaya style menu: from raw (sushi/sashimi), noodles, deep-fried dishes, all time classics and yakitori. \nThe food is fresh, well prepared and tasty.\nNo surprise this place is the preferred spot among Japanese tourists and expats alike.\nAbsolutely suggested for a casual but proper Japanese meal in town.\n\nNEW ENTRY IN THE Y&SFOOD! DA NANG DINING GUIDE 2024.\nRead more\nWritten October 29, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-04",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
